#      16          2083.3          5104.2          3020.8      59.2%
#
# **At the payload the control plane actually moves, over a real gRPC call, the
# codec is the MAJORITY of the CPU.** That is the premise this whole exploration
# rests on and it had not been measured end to end before: stages 1 to 3 timed
# the codec in isolation, and stage 4 timed the RPC without one in the loop.
#
# Two things this does NOT say. It does not say a native codec would recover
# that share -- cells A, B and C are within this harness's noise of each other,
# so on THIS host, where prost is already native, there is nothing to recover;
# the share is what a managed host's codec has to compete for. And it is a share
# of CPU on a loopback with a do-nothing server, so the denominator is as small
# as a real deployment's ever gets, which makes this an UPPER bound on the
# fraction, not a typical one.

