# HAZARDS (R9), and they are large here.
#   - FOUR vCPUs, with the server's two worker threads, each arm's runtime and
#     N host threads all on them. At 8 and 16 in flight the machine is
#     oversubscribed before the measurement starts, so these rows are a LOWER
#     bound and an upper bound on nothing. What survives is the arms' RELATIVE
#     behaviour under identical oversubscription.
#   - The server is in the same process and contends for the same four vCPUs,
#     so server cost is inside every number in every cell equally.
#   - CPU is process utime+stime at 10 ms resolution; the ROUND carries it and
#     the per-call figure is a division, not a per-call measurement.
#   - The windows are pinned now, so the wall column is no longer mostly
#     WINDOW_UPDATE latency. It is still a shared-box wall clock.
#   - No TLS, no retry, no metadata, no deadlines, no streaming, no failure
#     injection, no server-side measurement. **The RPC half's case is
#     BEHAVIOURAL and none of that behaviour is exercised here either.**
#   - Cancellation: `ak_call_cancel` exists and nothing in this harness calls
#     it. `design/SHAPES.md`'s carrier-thread row stays empty: Rust has no
#     carrier thread to pin (R8, report it empty rather than substitute).
